[John has been looking for a sample of vesicular basalt, a rock type that     
would indicate the presence of lava flows in the area as some of the          
geologists had expected. Vesicles are the imprints of gas bubbles that form   
near the surface of a cooling lava flow.]                                     
                                                                              
